# `fail` stores `cached` into what `new Error()` has just handed it: an object of a built-in class, of none of the program's layouts. `cached` of Links is stored into objects that arrive alone and stays unmarked.
# `origin` is stored into an object that Link has lost: it goes to the layout that has every name of the run.
# -- source: a-name-stored-into-an-object-of-a-built-in-class-says-nothing-of-other-layouts.ts
